  conName: GLP-1R
  pathwayNarrative: 
  npcDialogs: []
  conHeader: GLP-1R
  conSubHeader: Glucagon-like Peptide 1 Receptor
  conInfoPoints:
  - GLP-1R is 3-dimensional fold of a single polypeptide chain
  - GLP-1R has 7 transmembrane helices. These helices form a peptide-binding pocket
    that GLP1 sits in
  - A mutation here that differs between humans and rats dramatically changes the
    dynamics of GLP1-R's extracellular domain
  - Alpha helices are always right handed; Each turn is approximately 3.6 amino acids
    in length
  conInfoSources: 'Underwood et al, JBC 285, 723, 2010 ,

    Zhang et al, Nature,
    546, 248 2017. Figure S10'
  conPathway: Insulin Secretion
  conPDBNums: ' 5NX2- active, 5VAI- active'
  conFunction: "Messaging & Signaling. \nGLP-1R detects digestive activity via GLP-1."
  conDescription: A protein called GLP-1R, sitting in the cell's membrane, is the
    antenna. When the message GLP-1 sticks to it, it changes its shape.
  conOrigin: Generated from Ribosomes
  conDimensions: 'Volume: 51900 cubic Angstroms

    Radius: 23.1 Angstroms

    Height:
    112.454 Angstroms'
